# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# Exception: the committed *debug* keystore. It uses the standard public debug
# credentials (storepass/keypass "android", alias androiddebugkey) — the same
# well-known values as Flutter's auto-generated ~/.android/debug.keystore, so it
# carries NO security value. Committing it only makes the debug signature stable
# across CI builds, so sideloaded updates on test devices stop requiring an
# uninstall + Play Protect re-approval. NEVER commit a real release keystore.
!/app/holdable-debug.keystore
